## How this project is organized

This is a [GOTM](https://github.com/<owner>/gotm-framework-for-agentic-development)-orchestrated project. Goals are the why, Objectives are the what, Targets are the how-much, Milestones are the when (atomic execution passes — one Milestone equals one named output file).

The 11 discipline rules from `docs/03-discipline-rules.md` are binding for every Milestone execution:

1. GOTM.md is the single orchestration ledger — no in-chat planning.
2. Atomic Milestones — one M equals one execution pass equals one output file.
3. Milestone equals max context unit — read only the listed Inputs.
4. Foundation before drafts — gates block draft-tier work.
5. Ledger updates pair with file edits — same turn.
6. Chat is tight status — one to two sentences, ledger-referenced.
7. Temp docs liberally — write to the folder, not working memory.
8. Sub-numbering preserves atomicity — M1a, M1b each get their own row.
9. No ID recycling — sunset with strikethrough.
10. Subagent delegation uses the prescribed prompt template — Inputs only.
11. The ledger expands as we discover — write new scope before acting.

See [`decisions.md`](decisions.md) for the locked decisions and [`OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`](OPEN_QUESTIONS.md) for outstanding ratifications.

## Resuming after a pause

1. Read [`GOTM.md`](GOTM.md) top-to-bottom.
2. Read [`STATUS.md`](STATUS.md) for the gap ledger and foundation-gate state.
3. Read [`decisions.md`](decisions.md) for locked choices.
4. Read [`OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`](OPEN_QUESTIONS.md) for anything blocking work.
5. Identify the next eligible Milestone and execute it.

Do not re-litigate locked decisions. Do not plan in chat. The ledger has the plan.

